Disposition: fixes implemented; requested targeted gates pass. Full acceptance is pending the environment-limited checks below. No commit/push or packages/core edits.

## Changes

- HTTP boundary reads finishReason from the persisted turn/end matching this result's turnId (Core TurnResult does not expose it). Only error + length maps to 200; body preserves finalText/kind/steps/turnId and includes finishReason. Other errors remain 500.
- Web shows a localized, muted status and preserves the empty composer and partial response. HTTP fallback covers absent SSE; delayed SSE replaces that fallback to avoid duplicate output. Notice resets on new turn/session.
- Windows token open requests 0x2B including TOKEN_ADJUST_DEFAULT. Query integrity before relabel; never raise an already Low/Untrusted token. Failed relabel is tolerated only if an independent query proves Low or below; otherwise deny before process launch. No ACL changes or unrestricted fallback.

## Verification

- tsc -b: exit 0 ([log](tsc.log)).
- typecheck:tests: exit 0 ([log](typecheck-tests.log)).
- server + turn-status + sandbox tests: 4 files, 65 passed ([log](targeted.log)); includes real Core/persisted-event HTTP regression for empty and long length output and Windows C# compilation.
- test:web: 51 files, 424 passed ([log](test-web.log)).
- web production build --emptyOutDir false: passed ([log](web-build.log)); existing chunk-size advisory.
- Independent source review: no blockers ([review](review.md)).
- git diff --check: exit 0; git diff HEAD --stat -- packages/core: empty.
- Full test:all: see [log](test-all.log); final outcome to be recorded after completion.

## Limits and execution route

- Actual OpenCode CLI startup failed before task execution: EPERM opening C:\\work\\.local\\share\\opencode\\log\\opencode.log. Implementation and review therefore used PDW auxiliary host roles, not a successful OpenCode relay. No .pdw/config.json modification or permission bypass.
- Native dynamic token probe was rejected by PreToolUse: runtime-constructed types using Add-Type cannot be statically verified. Compiler-only test passed. A successful restricted child launch and observed native token integrity remain unverified; compilation/source assertions do not establish this.
- Browser tool: iab unavailable; inventory returned no apps/browsers. Real-browser notice verification remains unverified. Offline fixture is retained in browser-fixture.mjs (port 31855 checked free before launch, service stopped), with isolated system-temp state and no real provider network calls.
- No deletion commands were added except existing test cleanup of self-created system-temp directories. No core, package, lockfile, or model configuration changes.

## Next checks

Run OpenCode CLI, native restricted-token smoke and the browser length-limit interaction in a session with the required surfaces/access. Resolve full-suite failures separately if reproduced outside the sandbox. Existing investigation helper was not used as CLI evidence; it contains a pre-existing embedded credential and should be handled separately without reproducing it in logs.
